# Fix "Meta Device" Loading Error in Gemma Text Encoder

The current implementation of [AVGemmaTextEncoderModel](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/encoders/av_encoder.py#23-72) uses a simple linear projection ([GemmaFeaturesExtractorProjLinear](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/feature_extractor.py#8-44)) which is incompatible with the **Lightricks text_encoder patch** weights. The weights use a more complex `multi_modal_projector` with a bottleneck architecture.

## Proposed Changes

### ltx-core

#### [MODIFY] [feature_extractor.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/feature_extractor.py)
- [NEW] Add `GemmaFeaturesExtractorLightricks` class.
- Match the architecture found in the weights:
  - `mm_input_projection`: Linear(3840, 1152, bias=False)
  - `mm_soft_emb_norm`: Parameter(1152)
  - `mm_projector`: Sequential(Linear(1152, 3840), GeLU(), Linear(3840, 3840))
- **Crucial**: The `mm_input_projection` must handle the 49-layer aggregation or be applied after aggregation. Given the weights are `[1152, 3840]`, it likely applies *after* the layers are averaged or aggregated into a single 3840 vector. I will implement a default "aggregation then project" flow.

#### [MODIFY] [av_encoder.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/encoders/av_encoder.py)
- Update [AVGemmaTextEncoderModelConfigurator](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/encoders/av_encoder.py#74-85) to use `GemmaFeaturesExtractorLightricks`.
- Update `AV_GEMMA_TEXT_ENCODER_KEY_OPS` to map `multi_modal_projector.` weights to the new extractor attributes:
  - `multi_modal_projector.mm_input_projection_weight` -> `feature_extractor_linear.mm_input_projection.weight`
  - `multi_modal_projector.mm_soft_emb_norm.weight` -> `feature_extractor_linear.mm_soft_emb_norm`
  - `multi_modal_projector.mm_projector.0.weight` -> `feature_extractor_linear.mm_projector.0.weight`
  - ... and so on.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run the isolation test:
  ```powershell
  uv run python scripts/test_gemma_load.py
  ```
  - This should confirm that the model loads onto CPU without the `meta device` error and passes a simple forward inference.

### Manual Verification
- Once the text encoder is verified, run the hardware benchmark:
  ```powershell
  $env:HIGH_RAM_MODE="false"; uv run python scripts/bench_hardware.py --mode 16gb
  ```
